{
{{- /* Auth placeholders for @canva/opencode-plugin-llmproxy. Only rendered on
       work machines — .chezmoiignore skips this file on every other profile.

       opencode only invokes a plugin's auth.loader for providers that have an
       entry in auth.json (provider.ts: `if (!stored) continue`). Without these
       placeholders the plugin loads but never wires up its proxy transport,
       and the provider vanishes (`Provider not found: openai`).

       VPN (no CODER env):
         The plugin fetches a bearer token via `otter` and injects it in place
         of the "llmproxy" placeholder key.

       Coder devbox (CODER=true):
         The plugin uses AWS IMDS credentials with SigV4 signing instead of
         a bearer token. Having a placeholder key here breaks that path —
         opencode picks up the placeholder and bypasses SigV4. So we omit
         the amazon-bedrock entry entirely on Coder.

       google + openai route through the proxy in both modes (mTLS on Coder,
       VPN endpoint elsewhere), and both need the placeholder. */ -}}
{{- if eq "" (env "CODER") }}
  "amazon-bedrock": { "type": "api", "key": "llmproxy" },
{{- end }}
  "google": { "type": "api", "key": "llmproxy" },
  "openai": { "type": "api", "key": "llmproxy" }
}
